WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.300
If dopamine loss makes the STN overactive, what happens when you silence it?

2
00:00:09.233 --> 00:00:15.653
Picture a monkey made parkinsonian with MPTP, a toxin that kills dopamine neurons of

3
00:00:15.653 --> 00:00:16.653
the substantia nigra.

4
00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:19.477
Now lesion its left STN.

5
00:00:20.297 --> 00:00:21.477
Which way should movement change?

6
00:00:22.337 --> 00:00:23.537
And on which side of the body?

7
00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:30.680
Start with the sign.

8
00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:35.220
The STN excites the brake, and the brake inhibits the thalamus.

9
00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:38.060
That is one inhibition, an odd number.

10
00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:42.250
So when STN activity falls, the thalamus rises.

11
00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:44.570
The brake lifts, toward movement.

12
00:00:45.633 --> 00:00:50.873
Now the side. In the classic model, the left loop returns to the left cortex.

13
00:00:51.967 --> 00:00:55.547
Its commands then cross once, at the pyramidal decussation.

14
00:00:56.187 --> 00:00:58.067
So the change should appear on the right side.

15
00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:04.487
In 1990, Bergman, Wichmann and DeLong did this experiment in monkeys treated with

16
00:01:04.487 --> 00:01:05.487
MPTP.

17
00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:11.080
The parkinsonian signs improved on the side of the body opposite the lesion.

18
00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:13.250
The prediction held.

19
00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:18.750
This work helped make the STN a target for Parkinson's surgery, and for deep brain

20
00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:19.750
stimulation.

21
00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:22.250
But the count has a hard limit.

22
00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:27.390
In mice, both pathways become active together around the start of an action.

23
00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:32.840
When two routes pull in opposite directions, counting cannot say which one wins.

24
00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:35.560
That depends on how strong each route is.

25
00:01:37.383 --> 00:01:40.083
The model also gives no account of rest tremor.

26
00:01:40.743 --> 00:01:43.583
And how deep brain stimulation works is still unresolved.

27
00:01:44.767 --> 00:01:47.547
Count crossings for side and inhibitions for sign.

28
00:01:47.547 --> 00:01:50.067
Then check the count against the data.
